@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Medium requirements traceability diagram. Stakeholder
'                 requirements and system requirements in two packages, a
'                 deriveReqt chain between them, design elements satisfying
'                 system requirements, test cases verifying them, and an
'                 adjacency-matrix-style note table summarizing req -> test
'                 coverage.
'   usecase:      Teaching package partitioning of requirements, the deriveReqt
'                 chain across levels, and how to represent a traceability
'                 MATRIX as a note table alongside the graph view.
'   complexity:   medium
'   domain:       systems engineering / requirements management
' ============================================================================

title Requirements Traceability - Medium with Matrix

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' TEACHING NOTES
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' As requirements multiply, two views help:
'   1. The GRAPH (this diagram) shows how each requirement derives from a
'      stakeholder need, is satisfied by design, and verified by test.
'   2. The MATRIX (the note table below) shows req-vs-test coverage at a glance
'      — every cell with an X is a verify edge.
'
' Packages are used to organize requirements by source/abstraction level:
'   "Stakeholder Requirements" — what the customer asked for (the WHY).
'   "System Requirements"     — what the system must do (the WHAT, derived).
'
' deriveReqt vs derive: in strict SysML the dependency between two requirements
' is "deriveReqt" (a specialized refine/trace). Many tools render it as a dashed
' <<derive>> arrow. We use the stereotype form for portability.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

package "Stakeholder Requirements" {
  rectangle "STK-01\nUsers shall author\nUML diagrams in VR." as STK01 <<requirement>>
  rectangle "STK-02\nDiagrams shall be\nshareable as links."   as STK02 <<requirement>>
}

package "System Requirements" {
  rectangle "SYS-10\nProvide a 3D node\neditor canvas."        as SYS10 <<requirement>>
  rectangle "SYS-11\nSupport drag-link between\nnodes."         as SYS11 <<requirement>>
  rectangle "SYS-20\nGenerate a share URL per\ndiagram."        as SYS20 <<requirement>>
  rectangle "SYS-21\nPermissions: viewer vs\neditor roles."     as SYS21 <<requirement>>
}

' === deriveReqt chain: stakeholder -> system ===
SYS10 ..> STK01 : <<derive>>
SYS11 ..> STK01 : <<derive>>
SYS20 ..> STK02 : <<derive>>
SYS21 ..> STK02 : <<derive>>

' === Design elements (blocks/components) that satisfy system reqs ===
rectangle "Node Editor\nComponent" as NodeEditor <<component>>
rectangle "Sharing\nService"       as ShareSvc    <<component>>

NodeEditor ..> SYS10 : <<satisfy>>
NodeEditor ..> SYS11 : <<satisfy>>
ShareSvc   ..> SYS20 : <<satisfy>>
ShareSvc   ..> SYS21 : <<satisfy>>

' === Test cases that verify system reqs ===
rectangle "T-101 Canvas\nrender test"   as T101 <<testcase>>
rectangle "T-102 Link\ndrag test"       as T102 <<testcase>>
rectangle "T-201 Share\nURL test"       as T201 <<testcase>>
rectangle "T-202 Roles\npermission test" as T202 <<testcase>>

T101 ..> SYS10 : <<verify>>
T102 ..> SYS11 : <<verify>>
T201 ..> SYS20 : <<verify>>
T202 ..> SYS21 : <<verify>>

' === Adjacency-matrix-style note: req -> test coverage ===
note bottom of SYS21
  **Traceability Matrix (req x test)**
  X = verify edge exists
  --
  | Requirement | T-101 | T-102 | T-201 | T-202 |
  |-------------|:-----:|:-----:|:-----:|:-----:|
  | SYS-10      |  X    |       |       |       |
  | SYS-11      |       |  X    |       |       |
  | SYS-20      |       |       |  X    |       |
  | SYS-21      |       |       |       |  X    |
  --
  Gaps: a row with no X = unverified requirement.
  A requirement with no incoming satisfy = unsatisfied.
end note

note right of STK01
  **deriveReqt chain**
  STK-01 (the need)
    ^-- <<derive>> -- SYS-10
    ^-- <<derive>> -- SYS-11
  Each system requirement traces back to
  the stakeholder requirement it serves.
end note
@enduml
